  "lines": [
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Hi, what's brought you in today?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "I've got a stabbing pain under my left shoulder blade when I breathe in deep."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "When did it start?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "After a coughing fit with a cold, about ten days ago."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Any heart or lung problems in the past, or operations?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "I had previous surgery on my gallbladder."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "At least I think it was the gallbladder."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Any shortness of breath, chest pain at rest, or coughing up blood?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "None of that, no."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Let me have a look. Twist round to each side for me."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Twisting to the left gives you that sharp pain, and pressing on the seventh rib at the back brings it on too."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "I think you have a strained joint where the rib meets the spine, from all that coughing."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Breathe deep into the sore side ten times every hour so your lung stays clear."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Even though it catches?"},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Even though it catches, yes, a little discomfort is fine. If you get breathless or start feeling hot and shivery, see a GP that day."}
  ],
